<h2>Caruso Kitchens: A Dealer Doing It Right</h2>
<p><a href="https://carusokitchens.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Caruso Kitchens</a> has built a reputation for bringing thoughtful, design-forward cabinetry to their market — and this video is a perfect example of why. Instead of a staged showroom shot, the camera walks through one of their finished <a href="/brands/eclipse-cabinetry">Eclipse Cabinetry</a> projects in a homeowner's house. Real materials, smart finish pairings, and a design story you can actually see lived in.</p>
<p>What you'll see in the video: an installed Eclipse kitchen the way the client uses it day to day — door styles, finishes, hardware, and storage solutions in their natural habitat instead of next to a swatch deck. That's the difference between content that sells and content that just shows product.</p>

<h2>Dealers: Filming Your Installed Work Is Now Part of the Job</h2>
<p>The dealers growing fastest in 2026 have one thing in common — they're publishing their own content, and the highest-converting content isn't a showroom tour, it's a finished project. Not manufacturer stock photos. Not brochure shots. <em>Their own installs, on camera, in their own voice.</em></p>
<p>Why this matters more every quarter:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>The kitchen buying journey starts on a phone.</strong> Before a homeowner books a consultation, they've already scrolled Instagram, Pinterest, TikTok, and YouTube for hours. If your finished projects aren't there, you're invisible at the top of the funnel.</li>
  <li><strong>Real-home installs beat showroom shots for trust.</strong> A 45-second walkthrough of a finished kitchen in a real client's house earns more credibility than a month of static showroom posts. People want to see what their kitchen could actually look like — not a display.</li>
  <li><strong>Content is an appreciating asset.</strong> A single well-produced install video keeps generating leads, referrals, and designer inquiries long after it's published. Static ads stop working the day your budget runs out.</li>
  <li><strong>You become the authority in your market.</strong> The dealer with a library of finished Eclipse kitchens on video becomes "the Eclipse expert" in their region. Referrals follow authority.</li>
</ul>

